# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Secrets — never commit
.env
.kite_session_cache.json

# Generated output — csv/ and latest_volume_profile.json are deliberately NOT
# ignored: logs, caches and golden fixtures are kept locally as the evidence
# base that policy is scored against.
# Pre-move paths — kept so an older checkout can't commit a stray log. Leading
# slash is load-bearing: unanchored, these match at ANY depth and would silently
# re-ignore csv/alert_log.csv and csv/signal_log.csv.
/volume_profile_log.csv
/alert_log.csv
/alert_log.csv.bak
/signal_log.csv

# Dry-run output (BN_DRY_RUN=1). Disposable by construction — a dry run writes
# nothing outside this directory — and never evidence, so unlike csv/ it IS
# ignored. Also excluded from sync.sh already, which copies *.py only.
csv-dryrun/

# VS Code (keep launch.json/settings.json, ignore local overrides)
.vscode/*.local.json

# Test cache — no secrets, just churn; same reasoning as __pycache__ above.
.pytest_cache/

# Docs that name the live VM directly — external IP, SSH username, GCE
# instance name, or a personal Telegram chat ID. None of it is a credential
# (the IP is ephemeral and rotates on stop/start; the chat ID is meaningless
# without the bot token, which is already gitignored above), but together
# they're a map to a real, currently-live box, and a repo is forever even if
# a file is deleted from it later. Excluded rather than redacted — these are
# handover/runbook notes whose whole value IS the concrete values, so a
# placeholder version would stop being useful as documentation. Kept locally;
# regenerate a redacted equivalent if this project is ever handed to someone
# else.
/Markdowns/vm_handover.md
/Markdowns/deployment_runbook.md
/Markdowns/session_state_05sep.md
/Markdowns/bn_linux_migration.md
/vscode_handoff_prompt.md
